problem "The velocity of a particle is $(-i+4j)\\,\\text{km/h}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{h}.$ If the particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(2i+j)\\,{\\text{km/h}}^{2},$ find the velocity of the particle when $t=6\\,\\text{h}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nu=-i+4j,\\,a=2i+j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $t=6\\,\\text{h},$ the velocity of the particle will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\  & =(-i+4j)+(2i+j)(6) \\\\  & =(-i+4j)+(12i+6j) \\\\  & =(11i+10j)\\,\\text{km/h}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-136341/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7439a96f-07b1-5673-a103-af2c63c25d18"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-136341"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186129413 :question/answer-fields 17592186126284] {:db/id "q-136288/selection/ma-v1/b02a9ebbcb2e6cef7d28ea0a7011a89c7552c1f36d7b11f03a23c8d9895f0be3/15c9cce670706ec2711af369bfb332bbe496a816dfe986682d74fd5db476b8f5" :answer/id #uuid "c27fa1b4-0e14-5062-bc9c-d6ebd2e1bdc7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{67}\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-136288/selection/ma-v1/b02a9ebbcb2e6cef7d28ea0a7011a89c7552c1f36d7b11f03a23c8d9895f0be3/887cf19cbc20d31ee2679a94d8cdb0b8c4778db6eb63c21b4596748b72054749" :answer/id #uuid "17235203-bcb1-57d2-b17c-e6167bb4e9cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-136288/selection/ma-v1/b02a9ebbcb2e6cef7d28ea0a7011a89c7552c1f36d7b11f03a23c8d9895f0be3/8502b7d0f1335399c9d4f6773bbed87475718f56c5c275e31469365ccc58cc26" :answer/id #uuid "c281d91b-378b-517e-bd40-11cf26cf034f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqr